pull request: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/pull/2022""" .

obo:BFO_0000144 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "process profile"@en ;
    obo:BFO_0000179 "process-profile" ;
    obo:BFO_0000180 "ProcessProfile" ;
    obo:IAO_0000112 "On a somewhat higher level of complexity are what we shall call rate process profiles, which are the targets of selective abstraction focused not on determinate quality magnitudes plotted over time, but rather on certain ratios between these magnitudes and elapsed times. A speed process profile, for example, is represented by a graph plotting against time the ratio of distance covered per unit of time. Since rates may change, and since such changes, too, may have rates of change, we have to deal here with a hierarchy of process profile universals at successive levels"@en,
        "One important sub-family of rate process profiles is illustrated by the beat or frequency profiles of cyclical processes, illustrated by the 60 beats per minute beating process of John’s heart, or the 120 beats per minute drumming process involved in one of John’s performances in a rock band, and so on. Each such process includes what we shall call a beat process profile instance as part, a subtype of rate process profile in which the salient ratio is not distance covered but rather number of beat cycles per unit of time. Each beat process profile instance instantiates the determinable universal beat process profile. But it also instantiates multiple more specialized universals at lower levels of generality, selected from   rate process profilebeat process profileregular beat process profile3 bpm beat process profile4 bpm beat process profileirregular beat process profileincreasing beat process profileand so on.In the case of a regular beat process profile, a rate can be assigned in the simplest possible fashion by dividing the number of cycles by the length of the temporal region occupied by the beating process profile as a whole. Irregular process profiles of this sort, for example as identified in the clinic, or in the readings on an aircraft instrument panel, are often of diagnostic significance."@en,
        "The simplest type of process profiles are what we shall call ‘quality process profiles’, which are the process profiles which serve as the foci of the sort of selective abstraction that is involved when measurements are made of changes in single qualities, as illustrated, for example, by process profiles of mass, temperature, aortic pressure, and so on."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "b is a process_profile =Def. there is some process c such that b process_profile_of c (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [093-002])"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000600 "b process_profile_of c holds when b proper_occurrent_part_of c& there is some proper_occurrent_part d of c which has no parts in common with b & is mutually dependent on b& is such that b, c and d occupy the same temporal region (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [094-005])"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000602 "(forall (x y) (if (processProfileOf x y) (and (properContinuantPartOf x y) (exists (z t) (and (properOccurrentPartOf z y) (TemporalRegion t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion x t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion y t) (occupiesSpatioTemporalRegion z t) (not (exists (w) (and (occurrentPartOf w x) (occurrentPartOf w z))))))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [094-005] ",
        "(iff (ProcessProfile a) (exists (b) (and (Process b) (processProfileOf a b)))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [093-002] " ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000015 ;
    owl:disjointWith obo:BFO_0000182 .

obo:BFO_0000147 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "zero-dimensional continuant fiat boundary"@en ;
    obo:BFO_0000179 "0d-cf-boundary" ;
    obo:BFO_0000180 "ZeroDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary" ;
    obo:IAO_0000112 "the geographic North Pole"@en,
        "the point of origin of some spatial coordinate system."@en,
        "the quadripoint where the boundaries of Colorado, Utah, New Mexico, and Arizona meet"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "zero dimension continuant fiat boundaries are not spatial points. Considering the example 'the quadripoint where the boundaries of Colorado, Utah, New Mexico, and Arizona meet' : There are many frames in which that point is zooming through many points in space. Whereas, no matter what the frame, the quadripoint is always in the same relation to the boundaries of Colorado, Utah, New Mexico, and Arizona."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000600 "a zero-dimensional continuant fiat boundary is a fiat point whose location is defined in relation to some material entity. (axiom label in BFO2 Reference: [031-001])"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000602 "(iff (ZeroDimensionalContinuantFiatBoundary a) (and (ContinuantFiatBoundary a) (exists (b) (and (ZeroDimensionalSpatialRegion b) (forall (t) (locatedInAt a b t)))))) // axiom label in BFO2 CLIF: [031-001] " ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:bfo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000140 .

obo:RO_0002082 a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "simultaneous with"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172>,
        "David Osumi-Sutherland" ;
    rdfs:comment "t1 simultaneous_with t2 iff:=  t1 before_or_simultaneous_with t2  and not (t1 before t2)"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf obo:RO_0002081 .

obo:RO_0002086 a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ends after"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "David Osumi-Sutherland" ;
    rdfs:comment "X ends_after Y iff: end(Y) before_or_simultaneous_with end(X)"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf obo:RO_0002222 .

obo:RO_0002502 a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "depends on" ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso obo:BFO_0000169 ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty .

obo:RO_0004008 a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has primary output" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "p has primary output c if (a) p has output c and (b) the goal of process is to modify, produce, or transform c." ;
    oboInOwl:created_by <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165> ;
    oboInOwl:creation_date "2018-12-13T11:26:32+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf obo:RO_0002234,
        obo:RO_0004007 .

obo:RO_0004009 a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has primary input" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "p has primary input c if (a) p has input c and (b) the goal of process is to modify, consume, or transform c." ;
    oboInOwl:created_by <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165> ;
    oboInOwl:creation_date "2018-12-13T11:26:56+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf obo:RO_0002233,
        obo:RO_0004007 .

obo:UO_0000034 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "week" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "\"A time unit which is equal to 7 days.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:uo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:UO_1000034 .

obo:UO_0000035 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "month" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "\"A time unit which is approximately equal to the length of time of one of cycle of the moon's phases which in science is taken to be equal to 30 days.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:uo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:UO_1000035 .

obo:UO_0000185 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "degree" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "\"A plane angle unit which is equal to 1/360 of a full rotation or 1.7453310^[-2] rad.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:uo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:UO_1000185 .

obo:UO_0000188 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pi" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "\"A dimensionless unit which denoted an irrational real number, approximately equal to 3.14159 which is the ratio of a circle's circumference to its diameter in Euclidean geometry.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:uo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:UO_1000188 .

obo:UO_0000196 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pH" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "\"A dimensionless concentration notation which denotes the acidity of a solution in terms of activity of hydrogen ions (H+).\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:uo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:UO_1000196 .

obo:UO_0000224 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "kilowatt-hour" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "\"An energy unit which is equal to 1,000 watt-hours.\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]" ;
    obo:IAO_0000118 "kilowatt hours" ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "kWh" ;
    rdfs:comment "The original term from UO had neither an alternative term nor has_exact_synonym. It was added for OEO purposes to include the Eurostat spellings."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:uo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:UO_1000223 ;
    :OEO_00020426 """add eurostat alternative term and has_exact_synonym:
issue: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/issues/920
pull request: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/pull/924""" .

obo:UO_0000232 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "bit" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "\"An information unit which refers to a digit in the binary numeral system, which consists of base 2 digits (ie there are only 2 possible values: 0 or 1).\" [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:uo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:UO_1000232 .

obo:UO_0000280 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "rate unit" ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "\"A unit which represents a standard measurement occurrence of a process per unit time.\" [UOC:GVG]" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy obo:uo.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :OEO_00010490 ;
    :OEO_00020426 """make subclass of 'physical unit'
issue: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/issues/2135
pull request: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/pull/2141""" .

oboInOwl:created_by a owl:AnnotationProperty .

